      "writtenOn": "2018-04-19T15:46:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When I implemented this, it occurred to me that the enforcement model only really applies to project limits. It doesn\u0027t really have anything to do with the registered limits in a system, does it?\n\nIf not, then we could probably reuse the /v3/limit path and add a `model` resource under that, instead of adding a new path:\n\n  GET /v3/limit/model\n  HEAD /v3/limit/model\n\ninstead of:\n\n  GET /v3/limit_model\n  HEAD /v3/limit_model\n\nUnless there is a relationship between the enforcement model and the registered limit that I\u0027m not aware of. I kept the this specific patch as GET /v3/limit_model because that is what was documented in the Queens specification [0].\n\nI can propose a patch to update the specification if we decide to go that route.\n\n[0] http://specs.openstack.org/openstack/keystone-specs/specs/keystone/queens/limits-api.html#flat-hierarchy-enforcement",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "2ea55afb18195eba9b76680359bdc0f32ed34755",
